# NEGSC baseline -- what is generated, and why it is not tracked.
#
# Rule of thumb: anything that can be rebuilt from a tracked file plus the
# recorded environment is ignored. Anything needed to *explain* a number is
# tracked, however large the temptation to ignore it.

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# --- Environments ---------------------------------------------------------
# Conda envs live outside the repo (~/.conda/envs), so this only guards
# against someone creating a local venv by mistake.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- Data -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The 6.05 GB raw file and the 181 MB 3% cache are both rebuildable with
# make_cache.py. data_raw/cache_manifest.json IS tracked: it records the
# sha256, row and per-class counts, so any result can be tied back to the
# exact input that produced it.
*.csv
!data_raw/.gitkeep

# --- Model artifacts ------------------------------------------------------
# Weights are output, not source. A run is described by its manifest
# (outputs/run_*.json) and reproduced from a seed, not by shipping binaries.
*.pth
*.pt
*.ckpt
checkpoints/*
!checkpoints/.gitkeep

# --- Run output -----------------------------------------------------------
# Metrics, loss curves, confusion matrices and manifests for every run.
# Kept locally as the audit trail; regenerated per run.
outputs/
runs/

# --- Logs -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Build and test logs are evidence for one session, not the record. The
# decisions they justify live in ENV.md and ROADMAP.md.
*.log

# --- Notebooks ------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.nbconvert.ipynb

# --- Docs and records: tracked on purpose --------------------------------
# These are the project's memory -- decisions, environment and the paper
# comparison. Never ignore them; the negations below make that explicit even
# if a broader pattern is added later.
!README.md
!ROADMAP.md
!ENV.md
!DECISIONS.md
!DEVIATIONS.md
!RESULTS.md
!LIMITATIONS.md
!reference/REPAIR_DIFF.md